st.wistia.com L135: \nL136: cite94†Image L137: \nL138: Latest News\nL139: \nL140: 14/\nL141: 09\nL142: \nL143: 2026\nL144: \nL145: cite95†Lukfook Jewellery First Enters the UK Market with Grand Opening of New Shop in Westfield Stratford City, London Retail Network Expanded to 14 Countries and Regions L146: (14 September 2026) — Luk Fook Holdings (International) Limited (“Lukfook” or the “Group”) (Stock Code: 0590) is pleased to announce the grand opening of Lukfook Jewellery’s Shop at Westfield Stratford City, London, on 10 September. The grand opening ceremony featured guests of honour including Ms. Joey Ko, Director of the HKTDC for the UK, Nordics Ireland, Ms. Amy Lowe, Deputy General Manager of Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield Group, Mr.\nL147: Tony Hurley, Operations and Estate Manager of Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield Group. They were accompanied by Ms. Wong Hau Yeung, Shirley, Executive Director and Chief Operating Officer of Lukfook Group, Mr. Cheung Cheuk Kin, Billy, Senior Business Director of the Group, Mr. Cheung Chi Keung, Darwin, Property Director of the Group, Mr. Ricky Yiu, United Kingdom District Manager of Lukfook Jewellery, and Ms. Evana Wong, Head of Westfield Stratford City Shop to unveil the new shop with all distinguished guests.\nL148: Mr. Wong Wai Sheung, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Lukfook Group, said, “The Group set a new three-year strategic plan last year with the goal of expanding into three new overseas markets. As a core hub in Europe, the United Kingdom gathers international tourists and local consumers with high purchasing power, offering enormous market potential that serves as a key driver to realise this plan.\nL149: Looking ahead, the Group will continue to explore potential European markets, refine its regional retail network, capitalise on market opportunities, and further implement its corporate vision of 'Brand of Hong Kong, Sparkling the World’.” Westfield Stratford City is situated in a highly vibrant core neighborhood of London, boasting a prime location that integrates fashion, dining, and social experiences, making it immensely popular among local consumers and tourists alike.\nL150: The Group believes that, leveraging the shopping center's strong foot traffic advantage, this cooperation will generate significant synergy to showcase Lukfook Jewellery's exquisite craftsmanship and brand appeal to a broader audience of United Kingdom and international consumers. Address: Unit SU2037, Westfield Stratford City, Montfichet Road, Olympic Park, London, E201EJ, United Kingdom Ms. Wong Hau Yeung, Shirley, Executive Director and Chief Operating Officer of Lukfook Group (4th right), Ms.\nL151: Joey Ko, Director of the HKTDC for the UK, Nordics Ireland (4th left), Ms. Amy Lowe, Deputy General Manager, Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield Group (3rd right), Mr. Tony Hurley, Operations and Estate Manager of Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield Group (3rd left), Mr. Cheung Cheuk Kin, Billy, Senior Business Director of Lukfook Group (2nd right), Mr. Cheung Chi Keung, Darwin (2nd left), Property Director of the Group, Mr. Ricky Yiu, United Kingdom District Manager of Lukfook Jewellery (1st right) and Ms.\nL152: Evana Wong, Head of Westfield Stratford City Shop (1st left), officiated the ribbon-cutting ceremony ~End~\nL153: 07/\nL154: 09\nL155: \nL156: 2026\nL157: \nL158: cite96†Grand Opening of Lukfook Jewellery’s New Shop in Vincom Dong Khoi Shopping Centre Jointly Celebrating Brand's 35th Anniversary L159: (7 September 2026) — Luk Fook Holdings (International) Limited (“Lukfook” or the “Group”) (Stock Code: 0590) is pleased to announce the grand opening of Lukfook Jewellery’s Shop at Vincom Center Dong Khoi, Ho Chi Minh City, on 1 September. The grand opening ceremony featured guests of honour including Ms. Huyen Baby, Famous Artist, Ms. Pham Thi Thu Hien, General Director of Vincom Center Dong Khoi, Mr. Tan Timothy, Vice President of Sales Marketing Development of InterContinental Grand Ho Tram.\nL160: They were accompanied by Ms. Wong Hau Yeung, Shirley, Executive Director and Chief Operating Officer of Lukfook Group, Mr. Lin Chu Xiong, Mr. Lin Jia Tian, Ms. Nguyễn Hà, Mr. Wu Ming Song and Ms. He Xuan, Directors of Lukfook Jewellery Vietnam Shop, to unveil the new shop with all distinguished guests. Mr. Wong Wai Sheung, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Lukfook Group, said, “Lukfook has always been actively seeking overseas business opportunities.\nL161: Vietnam, as one of the most dynamic markets in Southeast Asia, has also become a key market for Lukfook to expand its overseas footprint. Coupled with the Group celebrating its milestone 35th anniversary on September 1, the opening of our Vincom Center Dong Khoi shop marks a delightful double celebrations.\nL162: Looking ahead, the Group will continue to deepen its footprint in Vietnam, expanding into high-potential cities like Da Nang and Nha Trang to build a comprehensive retail network, capitalise on market opportunities, and further realise its corporate vision of 'Brand of Hong Kong, Sparkling the World’.” The Group firmly believes that by pairing Ho Chi Minh City’s vibrant international appeal with Vincom Center Dong Khoi's prime location and heavy foot traffic, this partnership will yield strong synergies and showcase Lukfook Jewellery’s exceptional craftsmanship and brand prestige to a broader Vietnamese consumer base.\nL163: Address: Unit B1-17AB, Vincom Center Dong Khoi, No.72 Le Thanh Ton, Saigon Ward, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam Ms. Wong Hau Yeung, Shirley, Executive Director and Chief Operating Officer of Lukfook Group (4th right), Ms. Huyen Baby, Famous Artist (centre), Mr. Lin Jia Tian (4th left), Mr. Lin Chu Xiong (3rd right), Mr. Wu Ming Song (3rd left), Ms. Nguyễn Hà (2nd right), Ms. He Xuan (1st left), Directors of Lukfook Jewellery Vietnam Shop, Ms.\nL164: Pham Thi Thu Hien, General Director of Vincom Center Dong Khoi (2nd left) and Mr. Tan Timothy, Vice President of Sales Marketing Development of InterContinental Grand Ho Tram (1st right), officiated the ribbon-cutting ceremony ~End~\nL165: 31/\nL166: 08\nL167: \nL168: 2026\nL169: \nL170: cite97†Lukfook Group Shone Again at the “BOCHK Corporate Low-Carbon Environmental Leadership Awards” Garnered Triple Honours across “Services” and “Manufacturing” Sectors L171: (31 August 2026) — Luk Fook Holdings (International) Limited (\"Lukfook\" or the \"Group\") (Stock Code: 0590) is pleased to announce that the Group has again received prestigious recognitions at the “BOCHK Corporate Low-Carbon Environmental Leadership Awards”, being awarded the “EcoPartner” title in the “Services” sector for the seventh consecutive year.\nL172: Its subsidiary, Luk Fook Jewellery (Guangzhou) Company Limited, was named “EcoPartner” and received the “10 Years+ EcoPioneer Logo” in “Manufacturing” for the sixteenth consecutive year. Meanwhile, another subsidiary of the Group, Guangzhou Li Ying Jewellery Company Limited, participated for the fourth consecutive year and was honoured as an “EcoPartner” along with the “3 Years+ EcoPioneer Logo”.\nL173: These accolades commend the Group’s continuous contributions to driving green operations and low-carbon production across all operational aspects, spanning manufacturing, retail and administration. Mr. Wong Wai Sheung, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Lukfook Group, said, “The Group is honoured to have been commended at the ‘BOCHK Corporate Low-Carbon Environmental Leadership Awards’ over the years.\nL174: This demonstrates our commitment to eco-friendly practices and carbon reduction across operations, reflecting our long-term pledge to sustainability.\nL175: Looking ahead, the Group will continue to deepen its various environmental initiatives and work hand in hand with stakeholders to build a sustainable supply chain, striving together with all sectors of society to forge a green and low-carbon future.” Co-organised by the Federation of Hong Kong Industries and Bank of China (Hong Kong) since 2015, the “BOCHK Corporate Low-Carbon Environmental Leadership Awards” aims to encourage enterprises operating in the manufacturing, services and property management sectors across Hong Kong and the Pan-Pearl River Delta region to proactively implement environmental measures, reduce environmental pollution, and foster sustainable development.\nL176: Mr. Tse Moon Chuen, Non-executive Director of Lukfook Group, received the honour on behalf of the Group\nL177: cite98†More L178: \nL179: 14 /\nL180: 09\nL181: \nL182: 2026\nL183: \nL184: Lukfook Jewellery First Enters the UK Market with Grand Opening of New Shop in Westfield Stratford City, London Retail Network Expanded to 14 Countries and Regions\nL185: (14 September 2026) — Luk Fook Holdings (International) Limited (“Lukfook” or the “Group”) (Stock Code: 0590) is pleased to announce the grand opening of Lukfook Jewellery’s Shop at Westfield Stratford City, London, on 10 September. The grand opening ceremony featured guests of honour including Ms. Joey Ko, Director of the HKTDC for the UK, Nordics Ireland, Ms. Amy Lowe, Deputy General Manager of Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield Group, Mr.\nL186: Tony Hurley, Operations and Estate Manager of Unibail-Rodamco-Westfield Group. They were accompanied by Ms. Wong Hau Yeung, Shirley, Executive Director and Chief Operating Officer of Lukfook Group, Mr. Cheung Cheuk Kin, Billy, Senior Business Director of the Group, Mr. Cheung Chi Keung, Darwin, Property Director of the Group, Mr. Ricky Yiu, United Kingdom District Manager of Lukfook Jewellery, and Ms. Evana Wong, Head of Westfield Stratford City Shop to unveil the new shop with all distinguished guests.\nL187: Mr. Wong Wai Sheung, Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of Lukfook Group, said, “The Group set a new three-year strategic plan last year with the goal of expanding into three new overseas markets. As a core hub in Europe, the United Kingdom gathers international tourists and local consumers with high purc